Recycled Concrete Aggregates: A Review — McNeil and Kang (@mat-aggregate-recovery: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_7RV5XYMDWNA5KPVRYC7052WV8E
Katrina McNeil and Thomas H.-K. Kang. *Recycled Concrete Aggregates: A Review*. International Journal of Concrete Structures and Materials 7 (2013), 61–69. [Full public article and PDF](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40069-013-0032-5), DOI 10.1007/s40069-013-0032-5.

Read the entire article, then a complete original study underlying the material or member response you investigate. It connects adhered mortar, porosity, water absorption and aggregate history with mix behavior and structural observations. Compare actual mix proportions and conditioning before interpreting a replacement fraction.

Full text, selected aggregate/mix passages and the rights statement were inspected on 30 October 2026. The article states Creative Commons Attribution licensing; preserve author and component credits. Historical standards and the review's example acceptance thresholds are not a current universal specification. Its observed trends do not prove that every recovered aggregate is inferior or every proposed mix is suitable. Keep article media external.

